@page "/docs/skills"
@layout Layout.DocsLayout

<PageTitle>Agent skill · Klyroo.UI</PageTitle>
<div class="pg-prose">
    <p class="pg-eyebrow">AI</p>
    <h1>Agent skill</h1>
    <p class="pg-lead">Teach an AI coding agent how to build with Klyroo.UI: the conventions, the patterns, and when to ask the MCP server.</p>

    <h2>What it contains</h2>
    <p>
        The skill lives in <code>skills/klyroo-ui</code> of the repository. <code>SKILL.md</code> holds the core rules and a table that sends the agent to the
        reference file for its task, so it only loads what it needs:
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Guidelines</strong>: design system (tokens, colors, <code>Class</code> and <code>Ui</code>, global themes), choosing a component, conventions (render modes, the <code>Kly</code> prefix, binding, static rendering), forms.</li>
        <li><strong>Layouts</strong>: dashboard, docs, chat, editor, landing page.</li>
        <li><strong>Recipes</strong>: data tables, authentication, overlays, navigation.</li>
        <li><strong>Components</strong>: a quick reference of every component, generated from the same bundle as the MCP server.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The skill never lists parameters from memory. For the exact API it tells the agent to call the <a href="/docs/mcp">MCP server</a>.</p>

    <h2>Install</h2>
    <p>With the skills CLI, from the repository that hosts Klyroo.UI:</p>
    <CodeBlock Code="npx skills add OWNER/klyroo-ui" />
    <p>Or point your agent at the folder: copy <code>skills/klyroo-ui</code> into the skills directory of the tool, for Claude Code <code>.claude/skills/klyroo-ui</code> in a project or <code>~/.claude/skills/klyroo-ui</code> for every project.</p>
    <CodeBlock Code="cp -r skills/klyroo-ui .claude/skills/klyroo-ui" />
    <p>Then add the MCP server, so the skill and the tools work together: see <a href="/docs/mcp">MCP server</a>.</p>
</div>
